# THE HOLDING (ROADMAP slice 2 step 2; 46_settlements, Holding), through real
# keys: he sets down a holding with beds for six, goes back among a village that
# has seen him, and asks them to come; they bank the fire and walk there with
# him; and the night the plan comes for that village, nobody is behind the doors.
#
#   TOUR_TIMEOUT=600 TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/holding.tour --seed=1 --hour=10 --weather=clear:0 --give=timber:6,reeds:6,rag:6,scrap:4,driftwood:6
#
# The coast's first village (Oyster Row, at the spawn) has a working yard on seed 1, so
# its people see him in the first seconds and a snatch night is due for them.
coast calm
place spawn
wait 0.6
walk -1,1 2.6 run
wait 0.4
# A bunk for four and a hut for two: beds for the whole village.
tap holding
await app:holding 4
choose build_bunk
tap use
await made 8
choose build_hut
tap use
await made 8
tap pause
wait 0.6
shot 01-beds-for-six with holding
# Back among them. They have seen him: the ask is his to make.
village coast
wait 1.5
near holding_ask
wait 0.5
tap use
await talking 3
wait 0.4
shot 02-he-offers-them-his-beds with talking
tap use
await moved 3
wait 0.4
shot 03-they-will-walk with talking
tap use
wait 0.8
# They go while he is near and wait when he gets ahead (the Escort's walk): he
# goes to the holding, then turns back to stand between it and them, as a
# player who looks round for the people he is walking home does.
walkto holding 30
walk 1,-1 1.0
until walked_in 40
wait 0.8
shot 04-home-at-the-holding with holding
# Two days on, the morning after its small hours (a village is come for between
# one and four), while he is away at the works: the plan came, and found nobody.
place works
wait 0.6
hour 5 +2
await kept 5
village coast
wait 1.0
shot 05-nobody-behind-the-doors
